---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import GlossaryTerm from '../components/GlossaryTerm.astro';
import PrussiaMap from '../components/PrussiaMap.astro';
---

<Layout title="Kulturkampf & Fertility | The Secularization of Prussia">
	<main>
		<!-- Hero Section -->
		<section class="hero">
			<div class="hero-overlay"></div>
			<div class="hero-content">
				<span class="eyebrow">A PhD Research Monograph</span>
				<h1>The Iron & The Altar</h1>
				<p class="subtitle">Institutional Conflict, Secularization, and the Demographic Transition in 19th-Century Prussia</p>
				<div class="cta-group">
					<a href="/methods" class="btn primary">Methodology</a>
					<a href="/evidence" class="btn secondary">View Evidence</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Abstract Section -->
		<section class="abstract">
			<div class="container">
				<div class="abstract-card">
					<div class="abstract-header">
						<h2>Executive Abstract</h2>
						<div class="ornament"></div>
					</div>
					<div class="abstract-body">
						<p>
							This study investigates the <GlossaryTerm term="May Laws"><strong>Kulturkampf (1872–1878)</strong></GlossaryTerm>—Bismarck’s massive institutional assault on the Catholic Church—as an exogenous shock to the cost of child-rearing and institutional secularization. 
						</p>
						<p>
							Using a panel of 400+ Prussian counties, I employ a <GlossaryTerm term="Difference-in-Differences"><strong>Difference-in-Differences</strong></GlossaryTerm> strategy to measure how the dismantling of Catholic oversight over education, marriage, and welfare catalyzed a structural shift in fertility behavior.
						</p>

                        <PrussiaMap />
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Key Findings Grid -->
		<section class="findings">
			<div class="container">
				<h2 class="section-title">Central Findings</h2>
				<div class="findings-grid">
					<div class="finding-card">
						<div class="finding-value">-0.041***</div>
						<div class="finding-label">CBR Impact</div>
						<p>Average reduction in the Crude Birth Rate per 10 percentage point increase in Catholic share.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="finding-card">
						<div class="finding-value">+12%</div>
						<div class="finding-label">Illegitimacy Rise</div>
						<p>Increase in illegitimate births following the introduction of civil marriage in 1875.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="finding-card">
						<div class="finding-value">1887</div>
						<div class="finding-label">Persistence</div>
						<p>The fertility shock persisted even after the "Rollback" laws ended the conflict in the late 1880s.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- The Conflict Intro -->
		<section class="conflict-intro">
			<div class="container grid-2">
				<div class="text-content">
					<h2>A State Within a State</h2>
					<p>
						In 1871, the newly unified German Empire faced a internal rival: the Roman Catholic Church. Bismarck viewed the Church as a "state within a state" that held too much power over the private lives and education of Prussian citizens.
					</p>
					<p>
						The resulting **Kulturkampf** ("Culture Struggle") was more than a political dispute; it was a wholesale replacement of ecclesiastical oversight with state bureaucracy. By removing priests from schools and mandating civil marriage, the state inadvertently altered the microeconomic incentives of the household.
					</p>
					<a href="/context" class="text-link">Explore the Historical Context &rarr;</a>
				</div>
				<div class="visual-content">
					<div class="image-frame">
						<img src="/images/hero.png" alt="Prussian Conflict Visual" />
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

        <!-- Final CTA -->
        <section class="final-cta">
            <div class="container">
                <h3>Interested in the Reproducibility?</h3>
                <p>The entire data pipeline, from raw Galloway census files to the final spatial regressions, is open-source and modularized in Python.</p>
                <a href="https://github.com/AntonEbsen/Demography" target="_blank" class="btn primary">Explore GitHub Repository</a>
            </div>
        </section>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	/* Hero Section */
	.hero {
		position: relative;
		min-height: 90vh;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		background: url('/images/hero.png') center/cover no-repeat;
		padding: 4rem 2rem;
		text-align: center;
        overflow: hidden;
	}

	.hero-overlay {
		position: absolute;
		inset: 0;
		background: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(11, 12, 14, 0.4), rgba(11, 12, 14, 0.95));
	}

	.hero-content {
		position: relative;
		z-index: 1;
		max-width: 1000px;
	}

	.eyebrow {
		display: block;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.3rem;
		color: var(--accent);
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
		opacity: 0.8;
	}

	h1 {
		font-size: 5.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.02rem;
	}

	.subtitle {
		font-size: 1.6rem;
		font-family: var(--serif);
		max-width: 800px;
		margin: 0 auto 3rem;
		opacity: 0.9;
        font-style: italic;
	}

	.cta-group {
		display: flex;
		gap: 2rem;
		justify-content: center;
	}

	.btn {
		padding: 1.2rem 2.5rem;
		border-radius: 4px;
		text-decoration: none;
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.15rem;
		transition: all 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
	}

	.btn.primary {
		background: var(--accent);
		color: #000;
	}

	.btn.primary:hover {
		transform: translateY(-5px);
		box-shadow: 0 15px 30px rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.3);
	}

	.btn.secondary {
		border: 1px solid var(--accent);
		color: var(--accent);
	}

	.btn.secondary:hover {
		background: rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.1);
		transform: translateY(-3px);
	}

	/* Abstract Section */
	.abstract {
		background: #000;
        margin-top: -4rem;
        position: relative;
        z-index: 2;
	}

	.abstract-card {
		background: var(--surface);
		padding: 4rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		box-shadow: 0 30px 60px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
		border-radius: 4px;
	}

	.abstract-header {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 2rem;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.ornament {
		height: 1px;
		flex-grow: 1;
		background: linear-gradient(to right, var(--accent), transparent);
	}

	/* Findings Section */
	.findings-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
		gap: 3rem;
		margin-top: 3rem;
	}

	.finding-card {
		text-align: center;
		padding: 3rem 2rem;
		background: rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.03);
		border: 1px solid rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.1);
        transition: border-color 0.3s;
	}

    .finding-card:hover {
        border-color: var(--accent);
    }

	.finding-value {
		font-size: 3.5rem;
		font-family: var(--serif);
		color: var(--accent);
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	.finding-label {
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.2rem;
		opacity: 0.6;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}

	/* Conflict Intro */
	.grid-2 {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 0.8fr;
		gap: 5rem;
		align-items: center;
	}

	.image-frame {
		position: relative;
		padding: 1rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	.image-frame img {
		width: 100%;
		display: block;
        filter: grayscale(0.2) contrast(1.1);
	}

	.image-frame::after {
		content: '';
		position: absolute;
		inset: -1rem;
		border: 1px solid rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.1);
		z-index: -1;
	}

    .text-link {
        color: var(--accent);
        text-decoration: none;
        font-weight: 600;
        display: inline-block;
        margin-top: 1rem;
    }

    .text-link:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
    }

    /* Final CTA */
    .final-cta {
        text-align: center;
        background: radial-gradient(circle at center, #1a1c20, #000);
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
        padding: 6rem 2rem;
    }

    .final-cta h3 {
        font-size: 2.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .final-cta p {
        max-width: 600px;
        margin: 0 auto 3rem;
        opacity: 0.7;
    }

	@media (max-width: 900px) {
		h1 { font-size: 3.5rem; }
		.grid-2 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
		.hero-content { padding: 0 1rem; }
	}
</style>
